 score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Hinge Health, Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $9.0B market cap on $588M of annual revenue.","Gross margins of 80% are the starting point for assessing pricing power.","The business throws off $171M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 29 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.6%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 109% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 4.2% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 449% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":4.490740438377751},{"text":"Operating margins 93% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $60.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (25.6% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Hinge Health (HNGE) Stock May Be Fully Priced On Earnings Expectations","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/healthcare/nyse-hnge/hinge-health/news/hinge-health-hnge-stock-may-be-fully-priced-on-earnings-expe","date":"2026-11-23","timestamp":1795428507.46,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.791,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Hinge Health (HNGE) Could Be 27% Undervalued After Its Pullback To Support","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/healthcare/nyse-hnge/hinge-health/news/hinge-health-hnge-could-be-27-undervalued-after-its-pullback","date":"2026-11-21","timestamp":1795234794.697,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.904,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"HNGE Stock Surges Nearly 146% YTD: Can Its Growth Story Continue?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3032056/hnge-stock-surges-nearly-146-ytd-can-its-growth-story-continue?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog%7Cprice_surge_%2F_plunge-3032056","date":"2026-11-18","timestamp":1795020960.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Hinge Health (HNGE) Could Be 20% Undervalued As Profitability Reshapes The Narrative","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/healthcare/nyse-hnge/hinge-health/news/hinge-health-hnge-could-be-20-undervalued-as-prof